ate"><addressbook><name>KAIMAI, NORIMITSU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, SHIGEAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONO, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKITA, KOTARO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A microporous polyolefin film of a novel structure having high permeability which comprises a polyolefin (A) having a weight-average molecular weight of 5x10&lt;5&gt; or higher or a polyolefin composition (B) containing the polyolefin, characterized in that the average pore diameter gradually decreases from at least one side of the film toward the center thereof; and a process for producing the microporous polyolefin film which comprises extruding a solution comprising 10 to 50 wt.% polyolefin (A) having a weight-average molecular weight of 5x10&lt;5&gt; or higher or polyolefin composition (B) containing the polyolefin and 50 to 90 wt.% solvent and removing the solvent from the resultant gel-state extrudate, characterized by containing a step of treatment with a heated solvent.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un film micro-poreux de polyoléfine d'une nouvelle structure à forte perméabilité consistant en une polyoléfine (A) d'un poids moléculaire moyen de 5 x 10&lt;5&gt; ou plus, ou en une composition (B) contenant ladite polyoléfine, dont le diamètre moyen des pores décroît graduellement depuis au moins l'un des côtés en direction du centre, et sur un procédé de fabrication d'un film micro-poreux de polyoléfine consistant à extruder une solution comprenant de 10 à 50 % en poids de la polyoléfine (A) ou de la composition (B) contenant ladite polyoléfine et de 50 à 90 % en poids de solvant puis à extraire le solvant du produit extrudé à l'état de gel résultant, l'une des étapes du traitement s'effectuant avec un solvant chauffé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>